<title>THAILAND: Thai buyer may have bought US soybeans - traders.</title>
<headline>Thai buyer may have bought US soybeans - traders.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A major Thai feed producer may have been in the market for 15,000 tonnes of U.S. soybeans for October shipment, trade sources said Thursday.</p>
<p>The price was said to be around $335 per tonne c&amp;f Bangkok, they told Reuters.</p>
<p>The purchase might have been made as part of a government low-tariff programme, they said.</p>
<p>Thailand allowed 426,460 tonnes to be imported under the programme in all of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 650-0642</p>
